Focus order when modal opens: According to bootstrap modal, focus is trapped inside modal and initially set to the first focusable element (maybe the close button? Actually bootstrap's modal focuses on the first focusable element inside the modal, which is often the close button if it appears first. Indeed close button is first focusable element in modal-header.

Tab order inside modal: close button -> confirm-name input -> cancel button -> delete button. That seems plausible.

Thus shift+tab from close button should go to delete button (wrap). However currently shift+tab from close button goes to the modal element (which has tabindex="-1") maybe because bootstrap's focus trap logic prevents leaving modal and when shift+tab at start, it focuses the modal element itself to keep focus inside? Actually bootstrap's modal uses _enforceFocus to keep focus inside modal: on focusin event, if focus is outside modal, it returns focus to modal element. This may cause shift+tab from first element to focus the modal element (since focus would go outside to previous element (like the button that opened modal) but then enforceFocus brings focus back to modal element (the div). That matches observed: after shift+tab, focus is on #confirm (the modal). So the bug is that when shift+tab from first focusable element inside modal, instead of wrapping to last focusable element inside modal, it goes to modal element (due to enforceFocus). We need to adjust focus trap to wrap within modal's focusable elements.

Bootstrap's modal already handles focus trapping: When showing modal, it adds focusin listener that returns focus to modal if focus leaves. However it also tries to focus the modal element itself when shown? Actually in _showElement, if config.focus is true, they call this._enforceFocus() and then in transitionComplete they call this._element.focus() (focus the modal). That means after modal is shown, focus is set to the modal element (the div) not to first focusable element. Wait but observed before shift+tab shows focus on #confirm-close, meaning after modal shown, focus was on close button, not modal element. How did that happen? Let's check bootstrap code: In _showElement, after adding CLASS_NAME_SHOW, if this._config.focus then this._enforceFocus(). Then transitionComplete calls this._element.focus() if config.focus true. So focus goes to modal element after transition. However maybe because modal has tabindex="-1", calling focus() on it sets focus to the modal element but because it's not tabbable, the browser may then automatically move focus to first tabbable element inside? Not sure.

Nevertheless, the issue is that shift+tab from first focusable leads to modal element focus due to enforceFocus returning focus to modal when focus leaves modal (i.e., when trying to go outside). To fix, we need to modify _enforceFocus to instead wrap focus within modal's focusable elements when shift+tab at start or tab at end.

